The `useCallback` dependencies array includes `showConfirmModal` and `translate`, which are already stable hooks from `useConfirmModal()` and `useLocalize()` respectively. Including them unnecessarily causes the callback to be recreated when these values change (though they typically don't). However, `displayName` is NOT stable and should be included.

**Suggested fix:**
```typescript
const handleRemoveUser = useCallback(() => {
    showConfirmModal({
        danger: true,
        title: translate('workspace.people.removeRoomMemberButtonTitle'),
        prompt: translate('workspace.people.removeMemberPrompt', {memberName: displayName}),
        confirmText: translate('common.remove'),
        cancelText: translate('common.cancel'),
    }).then((result) => {
        if (result.action === ModalActions.CONFIRM) {
            removeFromRoom(report?.reportID, [accountID]);
            Navigation.goBack(backTo);
        }
    });
}, [displayName, report?.reportID, accountID, backTo]);
```

