Calling `isGroupSelected(group.transactions)` and `isGroupIndeterminate(group.transactions)` on every render performs expensive array operations (`.filter()`, `.map()`, `.every()`) for each group, even when selection hasn't changed.

**Suggested fix:** Pre-compute selection state for each group in a memoized Map:

```tsx
const groupSelectionState = useMemo(() => {
    const state = new Map<string, {isSelected: boolean; isIndeterminate: boolean}>();

    groupedTransactions.forEach(group => {
        const groupTransactionIDs = group.transactions
            .filter((t) => !isTransactionPendingDelete(t))
            .map((t) => t.transactionID);

        if (groupTransactionIDs.length === 0) {
            state.set(group.groupKey, {isSelected: false, isIndeterminate: false});
            return;
        }

        const selectedCount = groupTransactionIDs.filter((id) => selectedTransactionIDs.includes(id)).length;
        state.set(group.groupKey, {
            isSelected: selectedCount === groupTransactionIDs.length,
            isIndeterminate: selectedCount > 0 && selectedCount < groupTransactionIDs.length
        });
    });

    return state;
}, [groupedTransactions, selectedTransactionIDs]);

// Then in render:
<MoneyRequestReportGroupHeader
    isSelected={groupSelectionState.get(group.groupKey)?.isSelected ?? false}
    isIndeterminate={groupSelectionState.get(group.groupKey)?.isIndeterminate ?? false}
    // ... other props
/>
```

