const menuItems = useMemo(() => listItems.map((item) => ({
    key: item.key,
    shouldShowRightIcon: true,
    viewMode: CONST.OPTION_MODE.COMPACT,
    title: item.name,
    description: item.value,
    onPress: () => setSelectedField(item.field),
})), [listItems]);

// Then in render:
{menuItems.map((props) => (
    <MenuItem {...props} />
))}
```

Function objects passed as props should be memoized to prevent unnecessary re-renders. The callback created for `updateFilter` creates a new function reference on every render.

Consider memoizing the callback:

```tsx
const updateFilter = useCallback((selectedFilter: ListItem) => {
    const newValue = selectedFilter.isSelected ? null : selectedFilter.value;
    setSelectedItem(newValue);
}, []);
```

Objects passed as props should be properly memoized to prevent unnecessary re-renders. The `item.field` object creates a new reference on every render, potentially causing performance issues.

Consider memoizing the object or passing individual properties:

```tsx
const handlePress = useMemo(() => 
    listItems.map(item => ({
        ...item,
        onPress: () => setSelectedField(item.field),
    })), 
    [listItems]
);

// Then use:
{handlePress.map((item) => (
    <MenuItem
        key={item.key}
        shouldShowRightIcon
        viewMode={CONST.OPTION_MODE.COMPACT}

        description={item.value}
        onPress={item.onPress}
    />
))}
```

The `Object.values(fieldList ?? {}).map()` operation creates a new array on every render, and each mapped object contains a new object reference. This could cause unnecessary re-renders of child components.

**Suggested fix:**
```typescript
const listItems = useMemo(() => {
    return Object.values(fieldList ?? {}).map((field) => {
        const suffix = field.name.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ', '-');

        // Extract form values once to avoid repeated property access
        const formKey = `${CONST.SEARCH.REPORT_FIELD.DEFAULT_PREFIX}${suffix}` as const;
        const formValue = advancedFiltersForm?.[formKey];

        if (field.type === CONST.REPORT_FIELD_TYPES.DATE) {
            const onValue = advancedFiltersForm?.[`${CONST.SEARCH.REPORT_FIELD.ON_PREFIX}${suffix}`];
            const afterValue = advancedFiltersForm?.[`${CONST.SEARCH.REPORT_FIELD.AFTER_PREFIX}${suffix}`];
            const beforeValue = advancedFiltersForm?.[`${CONST.SEARCH.REPORT_FIELD.BEFORE_PREFIX}${suffix}`];

            const dateValues: string[] = [];
            if (onValue) {
                dateValues.push(isSearchDatePreset(onValue) ? translate(`search.filters.date.presets.${onValue}`) : translate('search.filters.date.on', {date: onValue}));
            }
            if (afterValue) {
                dateValues.push(translate('search.filters.date.after', {date: afterValue}));
            }
            if (beforeValue) {
                dateValues.push(translate('search.filters.date.before', {date: beforeValue}));
            }

            return {key: field.fieldID, name: field.name, value: dateValues.join(', '), field};
        }

        return {key: field.fieldID, name: field.name, value: formValue, field};
    });
}, [fieldList, advancedFiltersForm, translate]);
```

The issue is that individual form properties should be tracked in dependencies rather than the entire form object.

The `defaultDateValues` object is created on every render, which could cause unnecessary re-renders of the `DatePresetFilterBase` component.

**Suggested fix:**
```typescript
const defaultDateValues = useMemo(() => ({
    [CONST.SEARCH.DATE_MODIFIERS.ON]: searchAdvancedFiltersForm?.[dateOnKey],
    [CONST.SEARCH.DATE_MODIFIERS.BEFORE]: searchAdvancedFiltersForm?.[dateBeforeKey],
    [CONST.SEARCH.DATE_MODIFIERS.AFTER]: searchAdvancedFiltersForm?.[dateAfterKey],
}), [searchAdvancedFiltersForm?.[dateOnKey], searchAdvancedFiltersForm?.[dateBeforeKey], searchAdvancedFiltersForm?.[dateAfterKey]]);
```

